(:id "port/python/packet/constants" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python: TestPythonPacketCoreSurface" "internal/codegen/python: TestPythonPacketClose and TestPythonPacketCloseNegativeControl" "make packet-defaults-python packet-defaults-python-negative-control") :tested-revision "af721cf08812f617a28a1dca311f81e909969771" :note "Tested on Linux x86_64 with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 and pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2. Packet close reads and writes every inventoried valid packet pin, including framed and shared-stream concatenations, byte-identically; the generated-reader control fails by name. The defaults driver checks constructor values and the eight C++ default pins, with a planted constructor fault.")
